  "id": "decision-rule",
  "term": "decision rule",
  "definition": "A decision rule is a principle or pattern an individual uses to choose how to act. In this reciprocity context, it refers to a way of deciding whether to cooperate, and some decision rules are simpler and require less cognitive effort than others.",
